const PAIRTOBED_ALIASES = ()
const PAIRTOBED_REQUIRED = ((:a,), (:b,))

@doc raw"""
    BEDTools.Bindings.pairtobed(; options...)::Cmd

Report overlaps between a BEDPE file and a BED/GFF/VCF file.

The `bedtools pairtobed` command with `options`, checked against those that its help lists, to run with [`BEDTools.lines`](@ref) or any of Julia's process functions.
It needs `a` and `b`: `BEDTools.Bindings.pairtobed(a = …, b = …)`.
Its usage, in BEDTools 2.31.1, is `bedtools pairtobed [OPTIONS] -a <bedpe> -b <bed/gff/vcf>`.

An option of `true` is a flag, `false` and `nothing` leave it out, a vector gives it each element as an argument, and another value gives it that value.
An option with several spellings, such as a short and a long form, takes any one of them, and each emits its own.

Options:
- `a`: `<bedpe>`, from the usage line.
- `b`: `<bed/gff/vcf>`, from the usage line.
- `abam`: The A input file is in BAM format. Output will be BAM as well. Replaces -a. - Requires BAM to be grouped or sorted by query.
- `ubam`: Write uncompressed BAM output. Default writes compressed BAM.
- `bedpe`: When using BAM input (-abam), write output as BEDPE. The default is to write output in BAM when using -abam.
- `ed`: Use BAM total edit distance (NM tag) for BEDPE score. - Default for BEDPE is to use the minimum of of the two mapping qualities for the pair. - When -ed is used the total edit distance from the two mates is reported as the score.
- `f`: Minimum overlap required as fraction of A (e.g. 0.05). Default is 1E-9 (effectively 1bp).
- `s`: Require same strandedness when finding overlaps. Default is to ignore stand. Not applicable with -type inspan or -type outspan.
- `S`: Require different strandedness when finding overlaps. Default is to ignore stand. Not applicable with -type inspan or -type outspan.
- `type`: Approach to reporting overlaps between BEDPE and BED.

It also takes the general parameters of BEDTools, in [`BEDTools.Bindings.GENERAL_OPTIONS`](@ref), which come before the subcommand.
"""
function pairtobed(; options...)
    return build("pairtobed", PAIRTOBED_OPTIONS, PAIRTOBED_ALIASES, PAIRTOBED_REQUIRED; options...)
end

const PAIRTOPAIR_OPTIONS = (a = "-a", b = "-b", f = "-f", type = "-type", slop = "-slop", ss = "-ss", is = "-is", rdn = "-rdn")
const PAIRTOPAIR_ALIASES = ()
const PAIRTOPAIR_REQUIRED = ((:a,), (:b,))

@doc raw"""
    BEDTools.Bindings.pairtopair(; options...)::Cmd

Report overlaps between two paired-end BED files (BEDPE).

The `bedtools pairtopair` command with `options`, checked against those that its help lists, to run with [`BEDTools.lines`](@ref) or any of Julia's process functions.
It needs `a` and `b`: `BEDTools.Bindings.pairtopair(a = …, b = …)`.
Its usage, in BEDTools 2.31.1, is `bedtools pairtopair [OPTIONS] -a <BEDPE> -b <BEDPE>`.

An option of `true` is a flag, `false` and `nothing` leave it out, a vector gives it each element as an argument, and another value gives it that value.
An option with several spellings, such as a short and a long form, takes any one of them, and each emits its own.

Options:
- `a`: `<BEDPE>`, from the usage line.
- `b`: `<BEDPE>`, from the usage line.
- `f`: Minimum overlap required as fraction of A (e.g. 0.05). Default is 1E-9 (effectively 1bp).
- `type`: Approach to reporting overlaps between A and B.
- `slop`: The amount of slop (in b.p.). to be added to each footprint of A. *Note*: Slop is subtracted from start1 and start2 and added to end1 and end2.
- `ss`: Add slop based to each BEDPE footprint based on strand. - If strand is "+", slop is only added to the end coordinates. - If strand is "-", slop is only added to the start coordinates. - By default, slop is added in both directions.
- `is`: Ignore strands when searching for overlaps. - By default, strands are enforced.
- `rdn`: Require the hits to have different names (i.e. avoid self-hits). - By default, same names are allowed.

It also takes the general parameters of BEDTools, in [`BEDTools.Bindings.GENERAL_OPTIONS`](@ref), which come before the subcommand.
"""
function pairtopair(; options...)
    return build("pairtopair", PAIRTOPAIR_OPTIONS, PAIRTOPAIR_ALIASES, PAIRTOPAIR_REQUIRED; options...)
end

