@doc raw"""
    BEDTools.Bindings.bamtobed(; options...)::Cmd

Converts BAM alignments to BED6 or BEDPE format.

The `bedtools bamtobed` command with `options`, checked against those that its help lists, to run with [`BEDTools.lines`](@ref) or any of Julia's process functions.
It needs `i`: `BEDTools.Bindings.bamtobed(i = …)`.
Its usage, in BEDTools 2.31.1, is `bedtools bamtobed [OPTIONS] -i <bam>`.

An option of `true` is a flag, `false` and `nothing` leave it out, a vector gives it each element as an argument, and another value gives it that value.
An option with several spellings, such as a short and a long form, takes any one of them, and each emits its own.

Options:
- `i`: `<bam>`, from the usage line.
- `bedpe`: Write BEDPE format. - Requires BAM to be grouped or sorted by query.
- `mate1`: When writing BEDPE (-bedpe) format, always report mate one as the first BEDPE "block".
- `bed12`: Write "blocked" BED format (aka "BED12"). Forces -split.
- `split`: Report "split" BAM alignments as separate BED entries. Splits only on N CIGAR operations.
- `splitD`: Split alignments based on N and D CIGAR operators. Forces -split.
- `ed`: Use BAM edit distance (NM tag) for BED score. - Default for BED is to use mapping quality. - Default for BEDPE is to use the minimum of the two mapping qualities for the pair. - When -ed is used with -bedpe, the total edit distance from the two mates is reported.
- `tag`: Use other NUMERIC BAM alignment tag for BED score. - Default for BED is to use mapping quality. Disallowed with BEDPE output.
- `color`: An R,G,B string for the color used with BED12 format. Default is (255,0,0).
- `cigar`: Add the CIGAR string to the BED entry as a 7th column.

It also takes the general parameters of BEDTools, in [`BEDTools.Bindings.GENERAL_OPTIONS`](@ref), which come before the subcommand.
"""
function bamtobed(; options...)
    return build("bamtobed", BAMTOBED_OPTIONS, BAMTOBED_ALIASES, BAMTOBED_REQUIRED; options...)
end

