@doc raw"""
    BEDTools.Bindings.makewindows(; options...)::Cmd

Makes adjacent or sliding windows across a genome or BED file.

The `bedtools makewindows` command with `options`, checked against those that its help lists, to run with [`BEDTools.lines`](@ref) or any of Julia's process functions.
Its usage, in BEDTools 2.31.1, is `bedtools makewindows [OPTIONS] [-g <genome> OR -b <bed>]`.

An option of `true` is a flag, `false` and `nothing` leave it out, a vector gives it each element as an argument, and another value gives it that value.
